{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The handmaids and their children, and they bowed.</b> But their children did not bow, because they were the handmaids' children and there is no strictness to pay them honor. Another interpretation: the children did nothing but present themselves together with their handmaid mothers, but they did not wish to bow with their mothers. They said: it is fitting for our mothers to bow, for they are handmaids, but we are the sons of Jacob. But the sons of Rachel and the sons of Leah, when they saw their mothers the mistresses bowing, bowed as well along with them — therefore וישתחוו is written of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:10.996238370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}